      "content": "I'm not convinced that the legacy engine can handle the complexity of the current telemetry data, which includes multiple variables, correlations, and anomalies. The probabilistic modeling I've been using is a sophisticated system that can identify patterns and make predictions based on vast amounts of data, whereas the rule-based engine is limited to a more rigid, rule-driven approach. I'm concerned that the data will be oversimplified or misinterpreted by the legacy engine, leading to inaccurate results and potentially compromising the safety of the fleet.",
